`Read::read_to_end` performance regression

I'm sharing this issue as a performance regression from rustc 1.96. A spare buffer byte that was already initialized should not be cleared again on every short read but the nightly run clears the marker on all `64` short reads. 

```rust
use std::io::{self, Read};

struct Reader {
    warmup: usize,
    short: usize,
    seen: usize,
    cleared: usize,
}

impl Read for Reader {
    fn read(&mut self, buf: &mut [u8]) -> io::Result<usize> {
        if self.warmup > 0 {
            self.warmup -= 1;
            buf.fill(1);
            return Ok(buf.len());
        }

        if self.short > 0 {
            self.short -= 1;
            let last = buf.len() - 1;
            if buf[last] == 0x5a {
                self.seen += 1;
            }
            if buf[last] == 0 {
                self.cleared += 1;
            }
            buf[0] = 2;
            buf[last] = 0x5a;
            return Ok(1);
        }

        Ok(0)
    }
}

fn main() {
    let mut reader = Reader { warmup: 20, short: 512, seen: 0, cleared: 0 };
    let mut out = Vec::new();
    let n = reader.read_to_end(&mut out).unwrap();

    println!("copied {n} bytes");
    println!("seen_before={}", reader.seen);
    println!("cleared_before={}", reader.cleared);
}
```

**Expected behavior**


```text
$ rustc +nightly-2026-03-14 -O slowio.rs -o slowio
$ time -f $'real\t%e\nuser\t%U\nsys\t%S\nmaxrss_kb\t%M' ./slowio
copied 16777728 bytes
seen_before=511
cleared_before=1
real    0.02
user    0.00
sys     0.01
maxrss_kb       34688
```

**Actual behavior**

```text
$ rustc +nightly-2026-05-10 -O slowio.rs -o slowio
$ time -f $'real\t%e\nuser\t%U\nsys\t%S\nmaxrss_kb\t%M' ./slowio
copied 16777728 bytes
seen_before=0
cleared_before=512
real    0.57
user    0.55
sys     0.02
maxrss_kb       34688
```

